.\"                                      Hey, EMACS: -*- nroff -*-
.TH TCPSER 1 "June 2026" "tcpser 1.2.2"
.SH NAME
tcpser \- Hayes compatible modem emulator over TCP/IP
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B tcpser
\-d \fIdevice\fP [\-s \fIspeed\fP] [\fIoptions\fP] ...
.br
.B tcpser
\-v \fIport\fP [\-s \fIspeed\fP] [\fIoptions\fP] ...
.br
.B tcpser
\-d \fIdevice\fP \-Z
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBtcpser\fP turns a PC serial port into an emulated Hayes compatible modem that
uses TCP/IP for incoming and outgoing connections.  It can be used to allow
older applications and systems designed for modem use to operate on the
Internet.  Designed for hosting Commodore 64 BBS systems with SwiftLink,
Turbo232, GLINK232, and userport RS232 adapters.
.PP
This hardened fork adds a security gate (bot protection), persistent IP
blocklist, PETSCII pre-connect screens, and an RS232 analyzer mode for
diagnosing adapter wiring.
.SH OPTIONS
.SS "Serial Port"
.TP
.BI \-d " device"
Serial device (e.g. /dev/ttyUSB0).  Cannot be used with \-v.
.TP
.BI \-v " port"
Virtual RS232 via TCP (ip232 mode).  Cannot be used with \-d.
.TP
.BI \-s " speed"
Serial port speed (default: 38400).
.TP
.BI \-S " speed"
Speed reported in CONNECT message (defaults to \-s value).
.TP
.B \-I
Invert DCD pin.
.TP
.BI \-i " string"
Modem init string (omit AT prefix).
.SS "Network"
.TP
.BI \-p " port"
TCP listen port or address:port (default: 6400).
.TP
.BI \-n " number=address"
Phone book entry (e.g. \-n 5551212=bbs.example.com:23).
.TP
.BI \-D " address:port"
Direct connection.  Use \fB:\fP alone for receiver mode.
.SS "Security / Bot Gate"
.TP
.B \-x
Require client to press BACKSPACE twice within timeout before allowing
connection.  Accepts 0x08, 0x14, 0x7F variants (PETSCII/ASCII/VT).
.TP
.BI \-k " password"
Require password within timeout.  Input is PETSCII/ASCII normalized and
case-insensitive.  Use \fB\-k env:VARNAME\fP to read the password from the
named environment variable instead of the command line, keeping it out of
the process table (\fBps\fP).
.TP
.BI \-W " seconds"
Gate timeout in seconds (default: 20, maximum: 300).
.TP
.BI \-F " count"
Number of gate failures before permanent IP block (default: 3).
.TP
.BI \-P " file"
Pre-connect banner file.  Sent immediately after TCP accept, before
any gate or serial traffic.  Can be PETSCII or ANSI.
.TP
.BI \-G " file"
Access granted screen file.  Sent after successful gate.  If not
specified, a default green "ACCESS GRANTED" message is shown.
.TP
.BI \-E " command"
External command to execute asynchronously after successful gate.
Environment variable TCPSER_PEER_IP contains the caller's IP.
.SS "Event Files"
.TP
.BI \-a " file"
Send to serial (local) side upon answer.
.TP
.BI \-A " file"
Send to TCP (remote) side upon answer.
.TP
.BI \-c " file"
Send to serial (local) side upon connect.
.TP
.BI \-C " file"
Send to TCP (remote) side upon connect.
.TP
.BI \-N " file"
Send to TCP when no answer (after 10 rings).
.TP
.BI \-B " file"
Send to TCP when all modems are busy.
.TP
.BI \-T " file"
Send to TCP upon inactivity timeout.
.SS "Logging"
.TP
.BI \-l " level"
Log level: 0 (NONE), 1 (FATAL), 2 (ERROR), 3 (WARN), 4 (INFO),
5 (DEBUG), 6 (ENTER_EXIT), 7 (TRACE).  Default: 0.
.TP
.BI \-L " file"
Log to file (default: stderr).
.TP
.BI \-t " flags"
Trace flags (can be combined): m=modem in, M=modem out,
s=serial in, S=serial out, i=IP in, I=IP out.
.TP
.BI \-O " file"
Connection log in CSV format (timestamp,ip,result,duration,bytes_in,bytes_out).
The file is created with owner-only permissions (0600) as it records caller
IP addresses.
.TP
.BI \-Y " file"
Statistics file.  When set, connection counters are auto-saved every 60
seconds and on shutdown, and restored on startup.  Without \-Y, statistics
are not persisted.
.SS "Recovery / Limits"
.TP
.BI \-w " seconds"
BBS watchdog timeout (default: 120, 0 = off, maximum: 600).  If no serial
data arrives from the BBS within this many seconds after a caller
disconnects, tcpser toggles DTR/DCD (and ultimately sends a BREAK) to force
the BBS to notice carrier loss.
.TP
.BI \-m " minutes"
Maximum session time in minutes (default: 0 = unlimited).  Disconnects a
caller after this many minutes to prevent line hogging.
.SS "Monitoring / Notifications"
.TP
.B \-M
Live full-screen ASCII traffic monitor on stderr (colour).  Distinct from
\fB\-t M\fP, which only enables modem-output tracing.
.TP
.BI \-H " port"
Start the HTTP web dashboard and Prometheus \fB/metrics\fP endpoint on the
given port.  Binds to 127.0.0.1 by default; set \fBTCPSER_DASH_BIND\fP to
change the bind address and \fBTCPSER_DASH_TOKEN\fP to require a
\fB?token=\fP value on every request.
.TP
.BI \-e " url"
Webhook URL notified on CONNECTED, DISCONNECTED, GATE_FAIL and IP_BLOCKED
events (Discord/Slack/ntfy/generic JSON POST).  May be repeated for multiple
targets.  Requires the \fBcurl\fP binary on PATH.
.SS "Tools"
.TP
.B \-Z
RS232 analyzer mode.  Interactive diagnostic that probes control line
wiring, sweeps 90 combinations of baud rate, flow control, and parity,
detects the cartridge type (SwiftLink, Turbo232, GLINK232, userport),
and recommends the correct tcpser flags.  Requires \-d.
.TP
.B \-V
Print version and exit.
.TP
.B \-h
Show help summary and exit.
.SH NOTES
Options \-d/\-v can be repeated for multi-line BBS configurations.
Options \-s, \-S, \-i, and gate settings propagate to subsequent modems.
.PP
DCD defaults to always-asserted (equivalent to AT&C0) because all
6551 ACIA-based cartridges (SwiftLink, Turbo232, GLINK232) disable
their receiver when DCD is inactive.
.SH EXAMPLES
Basic BBS hosting:
.PP
.nf
tcpser -d /dev/ttyUSB0 -s 2400 -p 6400 -x
.fi
.PP
With password gate and custom screens:
.PP
.nf
tcpser -d /dev/ttyUSB0 -s 2400 -p 6400 -k "secret" \\
  -P data/prelogin.seq -G data/accessgranted.seq
.fi
.PP
Analyzer mode:
.PP
.nf
tcpser -d /dev/ttyUSB0 -s 2400 -Z
.fi
.SH FILES
.TP
.I data/tcpser.blocklist
Default persistent IP blocklist.  Override with TCPSER_BLOCKLIST
environment variable.
.TP
.I data/tcpser.allowlist
Trusted IPs that skip the blocklist, rate limiter and gate.  Override
with TCPSER_ALLOWLIST.
.TP
.I data/*.seq
PETSCII screen files for pre-connect banner, access granted, busy,
and backspace gate screens.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B TCPSER_BLOCKLIST
Path to the persistent IP blocklist file.
.TP
.B TCPSER_ALLOWLIST
Path to the IP allowlist file.
.TP
.B TCPSER_DASH_BIND
Bind address for the \fB\-H\fP web dashboard (default 127.0.0.1).  Set to
0.0.0.0 to expose it on all interfaces.
.TP
.B TCPSER_DASH_TOKEN
If set, the \fB\-H\fP web dashboard requires \fB?token=<value>\fP on every
request (constant-time comparison).
.TP
.B TCPSER_PEER_IP
Set by tcpser in the environment of the \fB\-E\fP gate-success script; holds
the caller's IP address.
.SH AUTHOR
Original tcpser by Jim Brain <brain@jbrain.com>.
.br
ip232 support by Anthony Tolle <atolle@gcns.com>.
.br
Security hardening and analyzer by GENESiS-PROJECT.
